q=json.loads((K/'queue.json').read_text());assert q['active_batch'] is None;assert not (B/'batch.json').exists();B.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
rows=[(390, 'pullum-on-the-cloth', 'Pullum on the cloth', 'The speaker remembers the local name, taste and small evidence of eating plums. Fruit beside a juice mark preserves the playful private appetite and domestic memory without inventing the speaker or a market documentary.', 'Original horizontal 3:2 warm matte oil-pastel and gouache still life, modest and close. Three small uneven red-purple plums rest loosely at the left on a folded piece of plain off-white cotton, one partly hidden behind another. One fruit has a small split in its skin; a modest red-purple juice mark has soaked into the cotton beside it, following the weave and a fold, not a decorative splash. Natural dull bloom on some skins, soft local highlights only; no lacquered perfect fruit, elaborate bowl, knife, lettering, hand or person. Cropped fabric lower left, quiet warm unadorned surface at right. Fruit sizes and shadows coherent. A slightly mischievous memory of taste, not a luxury food advertisement.'), (395, 'green-in-a-small-imprint', 'Green in a small imprint', 'The ending imagines tireless renewal through a tuft of grass in water held by a hoofprint. Keep that small scale and precarious life instead of illustrating the poem’s many deities and sacrificial images.', 'Original horizontal 3:2 close ground-level watercolor with a few graphite accents. In ordinary brown earth there is one shallow roughly oval cloven hoof depression, its two adjoining impressions softened at the edges by rain, holding a little still water. A tiny tuft of narrow green grass rises at the damp margin, roots meeting soil naturally. Only a few blades, unequal and crossing; no large flower or glowing seedling. Soil forms clumps and lightly collapsed edges, water follows the hollow with subdued sky reflection; perspective low but enough to see the basin. Rest of ground fades into quiet pale umber wash. No animal, blood, deity, human, footprints in a trail, text or ornament. Focus on modest ongoing renewal after strain; no dramatic miracle or cosmetic cracked-desert cliché.'), (400, 'cotton-wicks-for-small-lamps', 'Cotton wicks for small lamps', 'The tribute finds sacred generosity in humble daily acts and describes rolling cotton wicks. A small unfinished task suggests that care without fabricating a likeness of Sai of Shirdi or an authoritative shrine.', 'Original horizontal 3:2 sparse charcoal drawing with restrained terracotta watercolor. Low oblique view of a plain floor: at lower left one small unlit earthen diya and part of a second lamp cropped by the frame. Beside them a small loose pinch of raw cotton and two hand-rolled cotton wicks, one shorter and imperfectly tapered. One wick rests naturally along the lip of the nearer lamp with its end inside the shallow bowl. No oil spill, flame, smoke, human hands, portrait, altar, sacred symbols, garland, writing or gold. Lamps are simple clay with coherent rim and stable base, cotton soft with a few selectively drawn fibers, remaining right half quiet ivory-grey paper. An interrupted practical act of preparation, intimate and ungrand, never a staged devotional product display.')]
items=[]
